# ==== T-FMT-C · what KIND of statement sits in an inline suite slot
#
# AXIS (4 cells): call · var-decl · nested `if` · block-bearing child.
# The inline emitter delegates the slot to `format_block_stmts` WITHOUT an
# `indent()`, so a block-bearing child (`int x = match y:` + an indented
# suite) nests relative to the HEADER's indent — exactly as the author
# spelled it. An `indent()` here would push the nested suite one level too
# deep and break the fixpoint.
#
# RED pre-fix (recorded 2026-08-11): all four EXPLODED (the `Stmt::If`
# emitter had no inline path at all). The block-bearing cell additionally
# showed the collapse + spurious-blank pair from the expr-match `else`.

void kinds(int y):
    if true: print(1)
    if true: int a = y + 1
    if true: if false: print(2)
    if true: int x = match y:
        case 2:
            20
        else:
            30
    print(3)

void main():
    kinds(2)
